            harvest_time_unparsed: "Average pick July 3 in 2005-2011 observations; best fruit quality harvest in Massachusetts surmised around July 1; target harvest week first week in July",
            description: "Fruit Notes identifies Black Pearl as NY 8139 from Bob Andersen's former Cornell stone fruit breeding program, evaluated on Gisela 6 rootstock at UMass Cold Spring Orchard. Source notes: early to mid-season bloom in the May 6, 2011 bloom table, blooms early but slightly after Burgundy Pearl and before Ebony Pearl, heavy to very heavy annual yields, oblate-heart fruit shape, medium-long stem, darkest red skin among the three Pearl cherries, red flesh, 8.9 g average fruit weight, 13.1 percent soluble solids, cracking in wet Massachusetts years but somewhat less cracking than Burgundy Pearl and Ebony Pearl in drier years, attractive to birds because it is early, and the author's best success harvesting a good crop among the three"
